module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.comparison_whose_operands_share_a_producer

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data comparison_whose_operands_share_a_producer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "comparison_whose_operands_share_a_producer" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a comparison whose two operands have a common producer** (INVALID STATE: a check compares two values and refuses when they disagree, but one operand is DERIVED FROM THE OTHER, or both are derived from one source, inside the scope the check runs in. The comparison is well-formed, the refusal arm is typed and located, the subject is the right subject -- and no input can make the two sides differ, so the check is green by construction and carries no information about the property it names.",

    "**THE DISCRIMINATOR, IN ONE SENTENCE: the comparison's two operands have a common producer.** That is the whole test, it is decidable by reading the two operands back to their sources, and it is worth asking before the check is written rather than after it greens.",

    "HARM. It is not that the check is useless; it is that the check is CITED. A typed refusal arm with a name reads as coverage of the state it names, so the obligation it appears to discharge stops being looked for -- and the state it appears to catch is exactly the one that keeps flowing. DESIGN section 4b names the shape at the top rung: a check whose RED is unauthorable is 'worse than absent, because it will be cited as coverage'. The same section's oracle rule is the general form, stated for measurements: 'a measurement copied from the same current tree is not an oracle', and 'if automating the literal's update collapses the assertion to measure() == measure(), the manual update was the test's entire content'. This class is that rule applied to a CONTROL rather than to a literal.",

    "SPECIMEN ONE (2026-09-12, gunbc#11004, reviews 64177 and 64196, session calm-crane-722, both found by review and neither by the author). The compiler door's required-lens coverage join compares the registered lens roster against the observations collected from running the gates, and refuses the compile when they disagree. Both sides come from `required_compile_lens_roster()` inside one call: `run_required_lens_gates` folds the roster and stamps each witness with the `identity` and `grain` OF THE ROW IT IS FOLDING, and `required_lens_observations` drops any witness that is not a registration before the join is asked. So the observation list is a structural image of the roster. Four of the join's six arms -- `RegistrationUnobserved`, `ObservedAtWrongGrain`, `RootLensObservedMoreThanOnce`, `ObservationUnregistered` -- have no authorable RED at that door; only `RegistrationDuplicated` and `RequiredLensRosterEmpty` can fire. The annotation nevertheless claimed that 'an obligation that silently stopped executing stops the line', which is precisely the unauthorable case: an obligation stops executing by LEAVING THE ROSTER, and a join made of the roster cannot see that.",

    "SPECIMEN TWO, THE SAME FILE AND THE SAME NIGHT, which is what makes this recurring rather than singular. `CompileLens.identity` is authored on the row beside the `gate` it names and bound to it by nothing, and the coverage join closes over that identity field. Swapping two rows' gates, or repointing a gate at a different wrapper, leaves the join closed and the roster digest unchanged: the join's two sides are the authored name and a witness stamped FROM that same authored name. Two independent claims in one module, filed as one class because the mechanism is identical -- a second operand that inherits the first instead of witnessing it.",

    "WHY IT SURVIVES REVIEW AND AUTHORSHIP ALIKE. Every local property is correct: the arms are exhaustive, the refusals are typed and located, the fixture-grain witnesses for each arm are genuinely discriminating, and the author can point at a passing suite for all six. The defect is not in any operand, any arm, or any witness -- it is in the RELATIONSHIP between the two operands at one call site, which no single artifact displays. Both specimens above were written by an author who had, in the same file and the same week, correctly stated two other ceilings honestly.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, AND IT IS CHEAPER THAN THE ONE-QUESTION TEST IT GENERALISES: for each side of the comparison, name the DECLARATION THAT PRODUCED IT. If the two names are the same, or one is reachable from the other without leaving the call, the comparison cannot fail and whatever it is cited for is unestablished. Two mechanical tells: a fold that BUILDS the list it will later be joined against, and a witness stamped with a field copied from the row being checked rather than recovered from the thing that ran.",

    "DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS, CHECKED BEFORE FILING RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Not `roster_is_its_own_denominator`: there is NO second statement there at all, and the repair is to obtain one; here two statements exist and are compared, and the repair is to make one of them independent. Not `population_selector_that_cannot_admit_a_counterexample`: that is a defect in how a POPULATION was constructed, by a lexical proxy for the predicate; here the population is correct and stable and the defect is in the second OPERAND. Not `corroboration_without_an_independent_derivation_axis`: that is a property of the relationship between two human READERS, which no artifact records, so it carries ceiling 1 and no trigger; this one is mechanical, visible in the source at both call sites, and therefore decidable. Not `a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch`: there the control reads the right accessor against a WRONG SUBJECT, so a correct subject fixes it; here the subject is right and the comparison still cannot fail.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: MITIGATION BY REVIEW -- nothing refuses, and both specimens were found by reviewers reading a diff, neither by any executing check. An earlier draft of this receipt said `mitigatable` and justified it by pointing at the join's refusal arms firing at fixture grain. That is a fact about the SPECIMEN's join and not containment of THIS class: those arms discriminate a malformed observation set, and none of them can detect that a comparison's two operands share a producer. Nothing in the corpus asks that question, so there is no executed evidence of containment and naming a ladder rung here would be the inflation DESIGN section 4b(1) forbids -- the reported rung must equal the rung established by executed evidence, and for this class that evidence is a human reading two call sites.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed, and the reason is that operand provenance is a declaration-grain question the substrate already answers. Whether the two sides of a comparison trace to one producer is decidable by walking the expression graph the compiler holds -- the same Node tree the namespace authority reads -- so a lens can refuse a refusal-bearing comparison whose operands share a producer, without executing either. It is not structurally IMPOSSIBLE, because a comparison of two expressions is a legitimate construction in general and only the refusal-citing case is the defect.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY RATHER THAN AN ARTIFACT: provenance-aware comparison analysis -- the ability to ask, of a comparison that feeds a typed refusal, whether its operands share a producing declaration, and to refuse the program when they do. The narrower repair for specimen one is an INDEPENDENT OBSERVATION CHANNEL: a receipt carried out of the runner that executed the gates rather than a list re-derived from the roster it is compared against. That repair discharges the specimen and NOT the class, which is why it is named here as the specimen's trigger and not as this row's.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
